  "notes": {
    "devPreview": {
      "fill": "orange",
      "maxH": 380,
      "size": 24,
      "text": "FOR DEV: the preview window must show a REAL in-game firework.\n\nThe dots in the polaroid are a CSS stand-in made for this mockup. In the game, that window is a small live canvas running the actual engine: same particles, glow, gravity and fade as the sky.\n\nThe pipeline already exists. FireworkGame.openAdvancedCreator() + updateCreator() create a second Renderer2D + InstancedParticleSystem on #creator-canvas and relaunch new Firework(0, WORLD_LAUNCHER_Y, currentRecipeComponents, …) on a loop.\n\nTo do: mount #creator-canvas inside the polaroid photo (388×372) instead of hiding the game behind a full-screen scene. Keep the main game running under the dim. Relaunch right away on every edit. The Launch button fires the recipe from a real launcher in the main sky.\n\nThe Shape grid lists unlocked shapes only.",
      "w": 720,
      "x": 1520,
      "y": 980
    },
    "devPrototype": {
      "fill": "orange",
      "maxH": 736,
      "size": 24,
      "text": "FOR DEV: this prototype fakes the engine.\n\nSky bursts, the polaroid preview and every number here are stand-ins. Real fireworks, rates and costs come from the game (see the note under the Firework tab).\n\nUse it for flow and motion: panel in 300ms with a slight overshoot, panel out 170ms, toast 320ms, buy bounce 420ms, tab tilt 240ms, new tiles fade up 240ms.",
      "w": 653,
      "x": 6080,
      "y": 0
    },
